  abstract={This study addresses the information security challenges faced by South African banking sector by introducing a framework that uses knowledge sharing to strengthen information security. Built using the Design Science Research approach and guided by Social Exchange Theory and General Deterrence Theory, the framework highlights factors such as technology, skilled security staff, clear policies, awareness, vulnerabilities, attitudes, and management practices as key to improving information security. The framework was evaluated through semi-structured interviews with ten experts in the IT division of the selected Banking institution. The results of the semi-structured interviews shows that the framework can help overcome major security issues in the banking sector. Beyond adding to academic knowledge, the study offers practical guidance for creating safer, more resilient banking institutions and points to opportunities for future research.},
